# Prose and captured evidence. Prettier reflows HTML inside fenced code blocks,
# which silently rewrites verbatim samples of what the site actually returned.
# Formatting owns the code; it does not own the research record.
*.md

# Response fixtures, for the same reason one level closer to the bone: these files
# are evidence about what the server emits, and their value is fidelity. Prettier
# reformats the JavaScript inside an `onclick`, unquoting object keys — which is
# exactly the string `session.ts` parses to find the a4j submit trigger. A fixture
# that has been prettified is no longer a sample of the site; it is a sample of our
# formatter. The `.xml` fixtures escape today only because no parser is inferred
# for them, which is luck, not a rule — so the directory is excluded wholesale.
# `stub-transport.ts` is code and stays formatted via the negation below.
src/**/__fixtures__/*.html
src/**/__fixtures__/*.xml
src/**/__fixtures__/*.pdf
